    "result": "All tests are now passing! Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Governance test failure** \u2014 `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was not exported\n- The governance module imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` from `schema.js` but didn't export it as a named export\n- Fixed by adding named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `src/finetune/index.js`\n\n**2. Toxicity evaluation failure** \u2014 Parameter mismatch\n- The `toxicityMetric` function had signature `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but was being called with `(outputs, references)` from `runEvaluations`\n- This caused the references array to be interpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging the test inputs as toxic\n- Fixed by updating the signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms)` to match the contract other metrics follow, and wrapping bannedTerms in `toArray()` for defensive coding\n\n## Result\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files  \n\u2705 All existing public exports preserved and working  \n\u2705 No test files modified",
